[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3 uid="uid://c8phoboman001"]

; PHOBOMAN, SKINNED — bead godot-test1-9k9n.2 (epic `9k9n`, owner ruling
; 2026-09-18): the heavy HUMAN on MPFB2's `game_engine` rig, 23 bones, built by
; `scripts/build_hero.py --hero phoboman` (the source of record;
; `assets/models/characters/PROVENANCE.md` carries the row). The ten generated
; parts this scene used to instance are referenced nowhere here any more; the
; files themselves, and the generator that wrote them, retire in child 9k9n.3.
;
; THE SCENE IS THE FLAG (`scenes/characters/teibi.tscn` said it first): the
; Skeleton3D under `Body` is what makes `hero_rig.gd` hand him to
; `hero_rig_skeleton.gd` instead of `hero_rig_limbs.gd`, which is why this
; migration is a data change and `player_controller.gd`, `remote_avatar.gd`
; and `player_abilities.gd` change by zero lines (`player_animation.gd`'s
; GAITS row is retuned for human legs, the waddle kept — that is the one
; exception, and it is numbers, not code).
;
; THE UID IS LOAD-BEARING and stays `uid://c8phoboman001`:
; `player_controller.gd`'s CHARACTERS points at the PATH, but a changed uid
; makes Godot rewrite every reference that resolved this scene by uid, and warn
; while it does it.
;
; `Body` stays even though the mesh needs no wrapper: the landing squash writes
; Body.position.y, `capture_rest_pose()` reads Body.rotation and the caller
; writes the lean and sway there for BOTH rig kinds, so every hero scene in this
; game has one. The .glb instance carries NO basis — a SKINNED glTF is exported
; Y-up and placed by its own root node, so the Rx(-90) every UNRIGGED part
; scene applies would lay the hero on his face.
;
; NO BoneAttachment3D: the helmet, the dragon and the pho face are IN the mesh
; (`join_rigid` / `join_weighted` in `build_helmet` / `build_dragon`), so the
; gait's head bobble nods the whole dome with no prop node to seat. The 9ynx
; 1.1013 Body scale is GONE with the parts — the .glb is built at size
; (1.7992 m standing, PROVENANCE row).

